# package.provided — atoms Portage treats as already installed, so it neither
# builds them nor pulls their dependencies.
#
# virtual/tmpfiles: net-dialup/ppp (and mail-client/mutt via cyrus-sasl)
# `inherit tmpfiles`, gaining a dep on virtual/tmpfiles. On this no-systemd
# image that virtual resolves ONLY to sys-apps/systemd-utils[tmpfiles], whose
# ebuild REQUIRED_USE demands a python_single_target — but Python is excluded
# from this image, so emerge aborts at dependency resolution. The only other
# provider, sys-apps/seedfiles, is a keywordless -9999 live ebuild (bad for a
# reproducible/attested build); sys-apps/opentmpfiles was removed from ::gentoo.
#
# This disc has NO tmpfiles.d processor and its sysvinit does not run one, so the
# tmpfiles.d snippets ppp/etc. install (e.g. pppd.conf creating a /run dir) are
# inert regardless — pppd creates its own runtime dirs. Declaring the virtual as
# provided satisfies the dep without dragging in systemd-utils/Python and without
# changing any installed file. See memory: tmpfiles-systemd-utils-python-trap.
virtual/tmpfiles-0-r7
